  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result so far at 0.619 acc, and multiprofile with avgpool aggregation was the single largest gain observed (config_002 vs config_001: +0.106). However, we have only tested one aggregation strategy (avgpool) and one fusion strategy (concat), leaving uncertainty about whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can better exploit the multiprofile structure. Question: config_020 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model_setting, profile_setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion (concat) identical to config_018, cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why this is the best next step: multiprofile is the dominant performance driver, so how profiles are combined is the highest-leverage unresolved design choice. A single-variable comparison against our current best gives the clearest signal per experiment, and the result directly informs whether to invest further in aggregation (or pivot to RNA encoder / fusion / image encoder) under the limited budget."
}

